      "id": 1,
      "text": "Brookland's name came from a post office that started as Powell and was renamed Brookland in 1882, cementing the town's identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/brookland_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sprang up around the railroads in 1882, with two major lines arriving that year, turning it into a railroad hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/brookland_arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1900, Brookland boasted a stave mill, cotton gin, hotel, saloon, general stores, doctors, and a druggist, serving travelers and farmers alike.",
